# Not installed by hand any more: `observer_watchdog.sh --ensure-cron` (called by the
# killswitch init script at every boot, safe to run at any time) installs these lines
# idempotently, preserves foreign entries, and bumps the crontab dir mtime so busybox
# crond rescans without a restart. Manual append still works if you prefer.
# crond's native granularity is 1 minute, so four lines offset by `sleep` give ~15s
# effective polling (operator decision 2026-10-04: 15s, not 30s — the kill-switch's
# arm delay is bounded by this cadence) without a persistent daemon process.
* * * * * /etc/passwall2-presets/observer_watchdog.sh
* * * * * sleep 15; /etc/passwall2-presets/observer_watchdog.sh
* * * * * sleep 30; /etc/passwall2-presets/observer_watchdog.sh
* * * * * sleep 45; /etc/passwall2-presets/observer_watchdog.sh
